answer:
The standard minimum age for remote pilots in the open category is **16 years** [reg-2019-947 | Article 9].

However, **no minimum age** is required in the following situations:
* When operating in subcategory A1 with a C0 class drone that is a toy (within the meaning of Directive 2009/48/EC) [reg-2019-947 | Article 9];
* For privately-built drones with a maximum take-off mass of less than 250 g [reg-2019-947 | Article 9];
* When operating under the direct supervision of a remote pilot who is at least 16 years old and meets all competency requirements [reg-2019-947 | Article 9, easa-amc-gm | GM1 Article 9].

*Note:* Member States may lower the minimum age for the open category by up to 4 years based on a risk-based approach, though those lowered ages only apply on the territory of that Member State [reg-2019-947 | Article 9]. Furthermore, Member States can define UAS geographical zones that prohibit operations, require specific conditions, or restrict access [reg-2019-947 | Article 15].

